README.md-1-# Fibonacci spirals on cones
README.md-2-
README.md-3-Snapshot: 2026-10-14 (America/Los_Angeles).
README.md-4-
README.md-5-Cao Zexian's problem in *10000 Selected Problems in Sciences: Physics* (Science Press, 2009), pp. 541–543, asks whether the consecutive-Fibonacci counter-rotating spiral patterns observed in stressed Ag-core/silica-shell microstructures minimize elastic energy, and whether changing the size of identical disks packed toward a cone apex alternates the pattern's chirality. The source gives experimental motivation but no constitutive energy, boundary conditions, or mathematical definition of the admissible Fibonacci class. Global equilibrium, densest packing, and growth-selected metastable patterns are different questions.
README.md-6-
README.md-7-## Verdict
README.md-8-
README.md:9:**PARTIAL overall; COUNTEREXAMPLE for the precise fixed-golden-angle packing claim below.**
README.md-10-
README.md:11:**FRONTIER_METHOD: DELIVERY-READY for the scoped certificates; NOVELTY-UNCLEAR as a research contribution.** The original elastic-energy question and unrestricted sequential-growth chirality question remain open here, not fully solved. Known commensurate triangular cone crystals and classical phyllotaxis mathematics are the baseline, not discoveries of this project.
README.md-12-
README.md-13-### Precise formulations addressed
README.md-14-
README.md:15:1. **C1-Finite:** On the intrinsic cone obtained from a sector of angle `pi/3` by identifying its edges (half-angle `asin(1/6)`), constrain 183 centers to slant radii `10 <= r <= 20`. Maximize their minimum geodesic separation. The equal-area golden-angle placement
README.md:16:   `r_i^2 = 100 + 150*i/91`, `theta_i = 2*pi*i*(3-sqrt(5))/2`, `i=0,...,182`, is **not** a maximizer. A triangular-lattice quotient has minimum distance exactly 1; the golden placement has a pair with squared distance strictly below `77/100`. Unit-diameter disks in the former fit in the same frustum `9.5 <= r <= 20.5`. This is an apex-independent, finite certified comparison, not a certificate of the unrestricted optimum.
README.md:17:2. **C1-Bulk:** For `r_n=c*sqrt(n)` and that fixed golden divergence on a cone of sector angle `2*pi*beta`, any packing of equal embedded intrinsic disks centered on every point after any finite initial deletion has asymptotic density at most `pi/(2*sqrt(5))`. At `beta=1/6`, a triangular-lattice quotient, with all centers of slant radius at most 1 omitted, attains the global upper-asymptotic-density optimum `pi/(2*sqrt(3))`. The fixed-golden-angle ansatz therefore loses in the bulk too. The theorem does **not** exclude all deformed configurations whose contact graph happens to have Fibonacci counts.
README.md:18:3. **C2-Reduced:** In a specified local linearized golden-spiral model, the two shortest *Fibonacci-offset* families change consecutively and the handedness of the larger-count family alternates at explicitly derived thresholds. In an achiral energy model, reflection instead makes opposite-handed minima degenerate at every disk size. Neither fact proves size-driven alternation for the book's physical growth process.
