README.md-51-## Research decision
README.md-52-
README.md-53-A global basin-hopping search cannot strengthen the existing strict counterexample to the fixed ansatz; finding the unrestricted finite optimum is unnecessary to disprove it. The highest-value next action is to specify the actual Ag/silica elastic functional and growth constraints, then compare a relaxed Fibonacci-contact state against a seam-bearing crystal at the experimental cone angle. Without those assumptions, answering the broader book question from generic Riesz optimization would substitute a different physical problem.
README.md-54-
README.md:55:## Approved scoped target: sharp tail density (2026-10-14)
README.md-56-
README.md:57:After explicit approval to choose precise subproblems, the proposed continuation was the sharp tail separation of every constant-divergence Fermat spiral, not the physical elastic problem. **Screening verdict: ALREADY-SOLVED mathematical mechanism; Certification of its cone-tail transfer, not a new open-problem solution.** The newly located 2024 packing/Lagrange theorem already gives the density law `pi*mu(alpha)/2`, and the golden limiting distance appears in 2012 phyllotaxis work. See STATUS.md §6 and RESULTS.md §9.
README.md-58-
README.md-59-For every fixed `0<beta<=1`, `c>0`, and real divergence `alpha`,
README.md:60:`d_tail^2=2*pi*beta*c^2*liminf_(q->infinity) q*||q*alpha||`.
README.md:61:The supremum of equal-disk densities obtainable by deleting a finite prefix is exactly `pi*mu(alpha)/2`, with value zero for rational `alpha` and for `mu(alpha)=0`. Its maximum over divergences is the known `pi/(2*sqrt(5))`; therefore changing a constant divergence cannot close the triangular-density gap. Supremum is not necessarily attainment: at the golden divergence the endpoint diameter fails on every tail. This screened item no longer occupies an active “still-open” selection slot.
