STATUS.md:87:## 6. Approved scoped target: sharp tail density — prior-art screen
STATUS.md-88-
STATUS.md:89:The approved continuation asked for the exact tail separation/density of `r_n=c*sqrt(n), theta_n=2*pi*n*alpha` for every divergence. Its number-theoretic mechanism is **ALREADY-SOLVED**, not a justified new open selection:
STATUS.md-90-
STATUS.md:91:- **S. E. Graiff Zurita, B. Kane, R. Oishi-Tomiyasu**, *Packing theory derived from phyllotaxis and products of linear forms*, [arXiv:2106.12333v8](https://arxiv.org/html/2106.12333v8), 26 September 2024. **Theorem 1(2), equation (12)** explicitly states `liminf_(epsilon->0) Delta(L_(phi1,phi2,epsilon)) = pi/(2*LagrangeNumber(phi1))`; its proof identifies the reciprocal Lagrange number with `liminf q||q*phi1||`. Theorem 1(1) and Example 1 give `pi/(2*sqrt(5))`. This is a lattice-deformation theorem, not literally our cone-tail statement; Bacher's local-lattice analysis supplies the established context. The elementary transfer in RESULTS.md states and proves the exact geometric quantifiers rather than claiming the formula is new.
STATUS.md-92-- The related journal publication is **S. E. Graiff Zurita and R. Oishi-Tomiyasu**, *Constructive Approximation* **60**, 515–545 (2024), DOI [10.1007/s00365-024-09691-3](https://doi.org/10.1007/s00365-024-09691-3). The publisher lists two authors whereas the inspected arXiv versions list three. The theorem citation above is deliberately to the inspected arXiv version; full journal text was not accessible.
STATUS.md:93:- **Jean-François Sadoc, Nicolas Rivier, Jean Charvolin**, *Phyllotaxis: a non conventional crystalline solution to packing efficiency in situations with radial symmetry*, [arXiv:1201.1432v2](https://arxiv.org/html/1201.1432v2) (2012), §IV.3, equations (3)–(4), already derives golden neighboring-distance minima tending to `sqrt(2*pi/sqrt(5))`. Its local approximation is not an endpoint-attainment proof.
STATUS.md-94-- **Yohay Ailon Tevet**, *Chabauty Limits of Fermat Spirals*, [arXiv:2506.22863v2](https://arxiv.org/html/2506.22863v2) (2025), Theorems 1–2, characterizes asymptotic local lattices for badly approximable divergences. It is additional prior art, not an open-status certificate.
STATUS.md-95-- **A. Hurwitz**, *Ueber die angenäherte Darstellung der Irrationalzahlen durch rationale Brüche*, *Mathematische Annalen* **39**, 279–284 (1891), [original record](https://eudml.org/doc/157573), is the classical sharp `mu(alpha)<=1/sqrt(5)` baseline. The original bibliographic record was inspected; the sharp constant is also instantiated in the inspected 2024 theorem.
STATUS.md-96-
STATUS.md:97:Akiyama's Delone equivalence and Bacher's local-lattice result remain relevant but do not justify presenting this density mechanism as unresolved. The cone transfer is recorded as Certification of a known mechanism, with rational/zero cases and supremum-versus-attainment made explicit. No nearby model is invented to preserve a novelty claim; the active slot was reassigned to the separately approved parentage-deficit-five problem.

